    "created_at": "2016-09-26T10:04:52Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-09-26T10:04:52Z",
    "body": "You think \"either or both\" is better than just \"either\"? How often do we have \"either but not both\"? XOR is kinda unique and making OR more verbose seems weird. (And sometimes I think we use either for cases where both doesn't really make sense, e.g., when picking between two enum values.)\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
