    "created_at": "2016-09-26T12:22:34Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-09-26T12:22:34Z",
    "body": "I'm not convinced that's clear for \"or\"; the clear fix for \"foo and/or bar\" is not just \"foo or bar\", but instead wording like \"foo or bar, or both\", in my opinion.\n\n```\n$ grep -E \"\\\\bor\\\\s+both\" source\n   <li>One or both of the following, in the given order:\n  attribute, a <code data-x=\"attr-base-target\">target</code> attribute, or both.</p>\n  what content on the page to initially skip or provide on request (or both).</p>\nthe time include a powerful energy source coupled to one or both of\n   data-x=\"attr-embed-type\">type</code> attribute set (or both).</li>\n  again both missing or both have the same value.</p>\n     <td>One or both of the <code data-x=\"dom-video-videoWidth\">videoWidth</code> and <code\n  range <span data-x=\"\">0&nbsp;&le;&nbsp;<var>y</var>&nbsp;&lt;&nbsp;<var>y<sub>height</sub></var></span>. If one or both of <var>x<sub>width</sub></var> and <var>y<sub>height</sub></var> are zero, then the\n   an <span>intrinsic width</span> or <span>intrinsic height</span> (or both) equal to zero, then\n   <li><p>Optionally, <a href=\"#inform\">inform the user</a> that the caret or selection (or both)\n  the new <code>ImageData</code> object. If one or both of <var>sw</var> and <var>sh</var> are\n  the new <code>ImageData</code> object. If one or both of <var>sw</var> and <var>sh</var> are\n    <p>The user agent may display a message to the user or abort these steps (or both).</p>\n   <li><p>If either or both of <code data-x=\"dom-ImageBitmapOptions-resizeWidth\">resizeWidth</code>\n```\n\nSo how about consistent \"one or both\" instead of \"either or both\", and have it be OK to use \"either\" in unambiguous cases?\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
